# Objective 1.1: Compare and Contrast Various Types of Security Controls

## Control Categories (How it is implemented)
- **Technical (Logical):** Implemented via systems, software, or hardware (firewalls, encryption, MFA).
- **Managerial (Administrative):** Policies, governance, and risk management procedures (AUP, background checks).
- **Operational:** Executed by people rather than systems (security training, guard patrols, log review).
- **Physical:** Tangible barriers and environmental safeguards (fences, bollards, badge readers, locks).

---

## Security Controls Matrix (Category × Functional Type)

| Control Type | Technical (Logical) | Managerial (Administrative) | Operational | Physical |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Preventive**<br>*(Stops attack before it happens)* | Firewall rules, ACLs, encryption, MFA | Security policies, background checks, separation of duties | Security awareness training, onboarding procedures | Bollards, mantraps, badge readers, fences |
| **Deterrent**<br>*(Discourages attacker)* | Login warning banners | Threat of termination or legal action in AUP | Guard patrols, front-desk sign-in | Warning signs, visible CCTV, bright lighting |
| **Detective**<br>*(Identifies/alerts during or after)* | IDS, SIEM alerts, File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) | Log review policies, internal audits | Reviewing CCTV footage, guard rounds | Motion sensors, glass-break detectors |
| **Corrective**<br>*(Restores state after incident)* | Patching, antivirus quarantine, automated failover | Incident response plan, disaster recovery policy | Restoring from backups, rebooting affected hosts | Fire extinguishers, sprinklers |
| **Compensating**<br>*(Alternative when primary isn't feasible)* | Virtual patching (WAF rule) for legacy OS | Exception approval documentation | Manual dual-approval for legacy system access | Security guard stationed at a broken gate |
| **Directive**<br>*(Instructs behavior/compliance)* | Group Policy (GPO) enforcing screen lock | Acceptable Use Policy (AUP), password policy | Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) | "Authorized Personnel Only" / "Exit" signs |

---

## Key Exam Distinctions
- **Deterrent vs. Directive:** A sign reading *"Protected by 24/7 Video Surveillance"* is **Deterrent** (discourages action). A sign reading *"Employees Must Wear Badges"* is **Directive** (mandates a rule).
- **Technical vs. Operational:** A firewall blocking packets is **Technical** (automated system). An analyst reviewing firewall logs is **Operational** (human execution).
